      "marks": 3,
      "answer": "At $A$, $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3$ and $m_{AB}=-\\frac13$, so $AB$ is the normal.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "At $x=1\\frac12$, substitute into their derivative to show $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3$ — M1.\nGradient of $AB=\\frac{5\\frac12-3\\frac12}{1\\frac12-7\\frac12}=-\\frac13$ — M1; substitute into a correct gradient expression.\n$3(-\\frac13)=-1$, hence $AB$ is the normal — A1.\nAlternative: from tangent gradient 3 obtain perpendicular gradient $-\\frac13$ — M1; show that the perpendicular through $A$ has equation $y=-\\frac13x+6$ and contains $B(7.5,3.5)$ — M1; conclude $AB$ is the normal — A1.\nTotal: 3",
